      "side": 1,
      "message": "`\"core-public-stubs-system-modules\"` uses the [from-source](https://cs.android.com/search?q\u003dname.*core-lambda-stubs-for-system-modules%20f:%5C.bp\u0026sq\u003d) equivalent of `core-lambda-stubs-for-system-modules` and not a prebuilt (you might have been searching in Android.bp and not .bp)\n\nMore generally, previously we had (a lot of pseudocode)\n```\n my_system_modules\n  |          |\n  v          v\n stublib     nonstublib\n\nmy_system_modules.from-text\n  |                     |\n  v                     v\n stublib.from-text     nonstublib\n```\n\nIIUC, you have changed java_sdk_library to\n```\nstublib ---\u003e stublib.from-source (if --from-text is missing)\nstublib ---\u003e stublib.from-text (if --from-text is present)\n```\n\nThen, can the build graph be just\n```\n           my_system_modules\n  |                            |\n  v                            v\n stublib (source or text)     nonstublib\n\n```\n\nWhy do we need `my_system_modules.from-text` at all?",
